---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi3_56",
  "series": "Band VI 3 (1672-1676); durchgesehener Nachdruck 1980",
  "seq": 56,
  "text": "[[454.15]] <b>56. Methodus physica. Characteristica. Emendanda. Societas sive Ordo </b> <span>454.15;0:63:056:76!      :L:l^</span>.\n[[454.16]] SOCIETAS SIVE ORDO\n[[454.17]] Mai 1676 (?)\n[[455.1]] Methodus Physica. Characteristica. Emendanda. Societas sive Ordo.\n[[455.2]] Maji 1676.\n[[455.3]] Ex propositionibus quae rerum emendandarum causa fiunt, eas maxime amo,\n[[455.4]] quarum fructus viventibus nobis percipi posse spes est. Quanquam enim et gloriae et\n[[455.5]] posteritatis rationem habeat mens generosa, juvat tamen laborum suorum praemiis\n[[455.6]] frui vivum videntemque.\n[[455.7]] Certum est unum hominem non satis temporis habere posse ad omnia inveniendum,\n[[455.8]] quae a ratione pendent et certa methodo possunt inveniri; neque satis occasionum,\n[[455.9]] ad ea invenienda quae a casu pendent atque experimentis non semper obviis\n[[455.10]] discenda sunt.\n[[455.11]] Certum est si omnia utilia quae saltem unius oppidi, ne dicam provinciae, homines\n[[455.12]] sciunt aut experti sunt, in unum collecta breviterque exhibita essent, Thesaurum\n[[455.13]] nos incomparabilem habituros. Quid si plures nationes consentirent, imo quid si\n[[455.14]] (plurium) seculorum scientiam collectam haberemus?\n[[455.15]] Si omnia egregia quae homines sciunt aut sciverunt annotata atque cognita essent,\n[[455.16]] credo felices et plerisque malis atque incommodis, humanam vitam urgentibus\n[[455.17]] superiores essemus, vix enim morbus est, cui non certum aliquod atque exploratum\n[[455.18]] remedium aliquis ex populo norit.\n[[455.19]] Ex his patet homines non nisi propria negligentia esse infelices.\n[[455.20]] Si saltem omnia vere utilia atque realia quae in tot libris extant in unum collecta\n[[455.21]] exstarent atque indicum universalium ope in promtu essent, Thesaurum incredibilem\n[[455.22]] haberemus.\n[[456.1]] Saepe notavi egregia inventa quae pro novis habebantur postea in libris veteribus\n[[456.2]] fuisse reperta, sed neglecta aut ignorata.\n[[456.3]] Si paucorum aspectu similarium corporum natura nosceretur; ut salis communis,\n[[456.4]] nitri, aluminis, sulphuris, fuliginis, olei, vini, lactis, sanguinis, aliorumque nonnullorum;\n[[456.5]] pateret inde natura plerorumque aliorum corporum, quippe quae ex his\n[[456.6]] componantur aut generantur.\n[[456.7]] (Credibile est naturam corporum aspectu similarium, ut salis communis, nitri,\n[[456.8]] etc. tam esse simplicem, ut a nobis facillime intima eorum structura intelligeretur, si\n[[456.9]] quis angelus nobis eam vellet revelare.)\n[[456.10]] Credibile est si natura corporum ejusmodi similarium nobis innotesceret non\n[[456.11]] difficulter nos rationem reddituros omnium quae in ipsis apparent, imo praedicere\n[[456.12]] posse omnes eorum sive per se sumtorum, sive cum aliis mixtorum effectus.\n[[456.13]] Quemadmodum facile nobis est praedicere effectus machinae cujus structuram intelligimus.\n[[456.15]] Ex his sequitur facile nobis fore, ex non admodum multis experimentis intimam\n[[456.16]] eorum corporum derivare naturam. Nam si simplex est haec natura experimenta ex\n[[456.17]] ea facile sequi debent; et, si experimenta ex ea facile sequuntur, (debet) vicissim etiam\n[[456.18]] ipsa facile sequi per regressum ex sufficienti experimentorum numero. Talis regressus\n[[456.19]] fit in Algebra, et in omnibus aliis fieri posset quodam calculi mathematici genere,\n[[456.20]] si modo homines veram ratiocinandi artem tenerent.\n[[456.21]] Vera ratiocinandi ars in rebus difficilibus et nonnihil abstrusis, quales sunt physicae\n[[456.22]] frustra speratur, quamdiu non habetur ars characteristica sive lingua rationalis,\n[[456.23]] quae mirifice in compendium contrahit operationes mentis, et sola praestare potest in\n[[456.24]] Physicis, quod Algebra in Mathematicis.\n[[456.25]] Ars characteristica ostendet non tantum quomodo experimentis sit utendum, sed\n[[456.26]] et quaenam experimenta sint sumenda et ad determinandam rei subjectae naturam\n[[456.27]] sufficientia: (Prorsus) quemadmodum in vulgaribus illis artificiis per quae divinari\n[[456.28]] solet numerus quem aliquis sibi tacite proposuit, facile ab Algebrae perito dijudicare\n[[457.1]] potest, an ea quae sibi ab alio dicta sunt de occulto illo numero, sint ad eum eruendum\n[[457.2]] sufficientia.\n[[457.3]] Unus est modus per quem pauci homines delecti parvis sumtibus et exiguo tempore\n[[457.4]] res magnas pro scientiarum vitae utilium incremento praestare possunt, si aliqui\n[[457.5]] sint qui accuratissime ratiocinari possint, his vero materiam suppeditent alii tum qui\n[[457.6]] ex horum voto experimenta sumant, tum qui res praeclaras passim in libris aut apud\n[[457.7]] curiosos extantes colligant atque ordinent.\n[[457.8]] Necesse est autem qui talia moliantur eos ab aliis curis esse solutos, et vero\n[[457.9]] affectu in studia ferri, et a paucis dirigi; et Laboratorio atque Bibliotheca, et caeteris\n[[457.10]] ad sumtus in aliquot mercenarios et experimenta necessariis abunde instructos esse,\n[[457.11]] et de superiore loco protegi.\n[[457.12]] Cum multi adeo sint ordines et praeclarae fundationes, mirandum est neminem\n[[457.13]] (unquam) quicquam tale fundasse in quo cum religione etiam humani generis praesens\n[[457.14]] utilitas combinetur; si quis unquam tale fundaret institutum, is supra quam credi\n[[457.15]] potest obligaret (sibi) posteritatem veramque nomini suo immortalitatem pararet.\n[[457.16]] Tale genus Ordinis haud dubie in tanta seculi luce non tantum magno applausu\n[[457.17]] acciperetur, sed et mox necessariis undique subsidiis, legatis, fundationibus, exsplendesceret,\n[[457.18]] et per omnes nationes seclaque facile diffunderetur, ac cum sapientia\n[[457.19]] etiam pietatem propagaret.\n[[457.20]] Cum coenobia nonnulla tantis abundent divitiis, optandum esset quod illis superest\n[[457.21]] ultra victus commoditatem scientiarum verarum incrementis impendi, quibus\n[[457.22]] maxime gloria Dei celebratur.\n[[457.23]] Omne praeclarum (naturae) artificium experimento vel demonstratione detectum,\n[[457.24]] hymnus est verus et realis Deo cantatus, cujus admirationem auget.\n[[457.25]] Quanquam non dubitem fundationem qualem dixi, incredibiles aliquando successus\n[[457.26]] habituram, et venturum esse tempus quo sapientiores, quam nunc sunt homines,\n[[458.1]] superfluas opes verae felicitatis incrementis impendent, quoniam tamen sub\n[[458.2]] initium monui, me de illis tantum dicturum, quorum fructus viventibus nobis percipi\n[[458.3]] possint, ideo hoc unum conclusionis loco adjicere suffecerit:\n[[458.4]] Si adhibeantur in hunc usum pauci homines sed selecti, quorum alii ratiocinandi\n[[458.5]] vi, alii experiundi industria, alii colligendi sedulitate valeant, et necessariis ad omnia\n[[458.6]] in eam rem profutura sumtibus abundent; et vero affectu ad instituti incrementum\n[[458.7]] conspirent; ausim dicere, plus eos uno decennio effecturos, quam alioqui totum genus\n[[458.8]] humanum tumultuariis sparsisque multorum seculorum laboribus possit. Unde quis\n[[458.9]] fructus omnes quae gloria Protectorem atque fundatorem maneat facile est judicare.\n",
  "number": "56.",
  "title": "Methodus physica. Characteristica. Emendanda. Societas sive Ordo",
  "date": ""
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:56. Methodus physica. Characteristica. Emendanda. Societas sive Ordo 454.15;0:63:056:76! :L:l^. SOCIETAS SIVE ORDO Mai 1676 (?) Methodus Physica. Characteristica. Emendanda. Societas sive Ordo. Maji 1676. Ex propositionibus quae rerum emendandarum causa fiunt, eas maxime amo, quarum fructus viventib...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>